# Review gate for this repository.
#
# Matches the package repo (Frisian-MCP/frisian-mcp), which uses the same
# single global rule and the same team.
#
# ── WHY ONE GLOBAL RULE AND NOT PER-PATH GLOBS ─────────────────────────────
#
# An earlier version of this file listed the publish-triggering paths
# explicitly — /.github/workflows/, /nautobot/, /common/, /paperless/ — with
# the stated intent of keeping them identical to the `paths:` filter on each
# workflow's `push: branches: [main]` trigger, so that "a change that can cause
# a publish is a change that needs a review" was true rather than aspirational.
#
# That intent was right and the mechanism drifted anyway: `netbox/` was added as
# a third host and never made it into the list, so every change to it was
# unowned. A rule that has to be updated in two places whenever a host is added
# will eventually be updated in one.
#
# `*` cannot drift. It already covers all three hosts and any fourth, and it is
# a superset of every workflow `paths:` filter, so the guarantee holds by
# construction instead of by remembering.
#
# ── WHY THE TEAM AND NOT INDIVIDUAL HANDLES ────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️ A team with NO access to the repository is dropped from CODEOWNERS
# SILENTLY — no error on the pull request, no owner assigned, and a "require
# review from Code Owners" rule then finds nobody to require. This file
# previously listed five individuals for exactly that reason, measured
# 2026-08-25, when `/repos/Frisian-MCP/frisian-mcp-demo/teams` was empty.
#
# That is no longer true. Re-measured 2026-08-31:
#
#     gh api /repos/Frisian-MCP/frisian-mcp-demo/teams
#       -> core-maintainers: push
#
# So the team resolves here now. It is preferred over handles because a roster
# written into a file goes stale, and because one of the maintainer handles has
# a near-identical impostor differing by a single letter — naming the team
# removes the chance of typing the wrong one into an access control.
#
# ── VERIFYING, AFTER ANY CHANGE TO THIS FILE ───────────────────────────────
#
# Do not assume an entry resolved. Ask GitHub:
#
#     gh api /repos/Frisian-MCP/frisian-mcp-demo/codeowners/errors
#
# An empty `errors` array is the confirmation. That endpoint is the check
# precisely because the failure mode above is silent.
#
# ── THIS FILE IS ONLY HALF THE CONTROL ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# It names who must approve; it does not require the approval. That comes from
# a ruleset on `main` with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. Without
# one, this file is documentation.

# Global owner - all files
* @Frisian-MCP/core-maintainers
